From 70e78630ccf0958593b29050efff55861c7c2f1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@example.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 18:09:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add 1-on-1 video calling to the chat widget

- database/migration_chat_video_calls.sql: dbo.ChatCalls (one row per
  call attempt, status ringing -> accepted/declined/missed -> ended)
  and dbo.ChatCallSignals (trickled ICE candidates). Gated separately
  from the base chat migration so existing installs don't need to run
  it to keep using chat - only the call_* actions require it.
- app/models/Chat.php: startCall/getIncomingCalls/getCallStatus/
  answerCall/declineCall/endCall/addIceCandidate/getIceCandidates.
  Calls are 1-on-1 only (direct conversations) - a call to everyone in
  the shared General channel would need real multi-party (mesh/SFU)
  infrastructure this app doesn't have.
- app/controllers/ChatController.php: call_start, call_incoming (polled
  globally every 3s so an incoming call shows up wherever the callee
  is in the app, not just inside an open thread), call_answer,
  call_decline, call_end, call_status, call_ice_candidate,
  call_ice_candidates.
- assets/js/chat.js: WebRTC calling using a public STUN server
  (stun.l.google.com) - actual audio/video goes directly between the
  two browsers once connected, never through this server. A video-call
  button appears in the header of any direct (1-on-1) thread; an
  incoming call shows a banner with a simple WebAudio ringtone,
  Accept/Decline, then a full-screen call overlay with mute/camera
  toggle and hang up.
- includes/chat-widget.php, assets/css/style.css: the call button,
  incoming-call banner, and call overlay markup/styling.

Limitation: only a STUN server is configured, no TURN relay. Two users
behind restrictive/symmetric NATs (common on some corporate firewalls,
different mobile carriers, etc.) may fail to connect peer-to-peer
without one - that needs separate TURN infrastructure (e.g. coturn)
this app doesn't provide.
